<header><b>OTHERWISE<span class="dot">.</span></b><small>0.4 / THE FIRST HUMAN</small></header><main><div class="eyebrow">A little peace of mind</div><h1>Your message stays yours.<br>Otherwise...</h1><p class="intro">Keep a Capsule safe by checking in. If you miss a scheduled check-in, its release can begin. This laboratory uses a synthetic message and simulated delivery.</p>
<div class="grid"><section class="card"><h2>Your Solo Capsule</h2><div id="state" role="status">Ready when you are</div><p id="notice" aria-live="polite">Create a practice Capsule, save your recovery kit, then arm it.</p><div id="schedule"></div><div id="create-fields"><label>Check-in window, seconds <input id="seconds" type="number" value="120" min="10" max="86400"></label><label>Number of check-ins <input id="rounds" type="number" value="2" min="1" max="8"></label></div>
<button onclick="act('create')">Create practice Capsule</button><button id="download" class="secondary" onclick="download()">Save recovery kit</button><button id="arm" onclick="act('arm')" disabled>Arm Capsule</button><button id="checkin" onclick="act('checkin')" disabled>I'm here</button><button id="status" class="secondary" onclick="act('status')">Refresh status</button><button id="disarm" class="secondary" onclick="act('disarm')" disabled>Disarm</button>
<label class="file">Restore recovery kit <input type="file" accept="application/json" id="restore" hidden></label><details><summary>Practice a missed check-in</summary><p>Wait until every window and its five-second grace have closed, then evaluate. Disarm early: once closure begins, disarm may already be unavailable.</p><button onclick="act('evaluate')">Evaluate release</button><button class="secondary" onclick="act('simulate')">Simulate delivery</button></details></section>
<aside class="card"><h2>Your independent proof</h2><p>Your browser verifies witness signatures before confirming a check-in. Your recovery kit lets the standalone client operate even if this application disappears.</p><p><b id="ack">No verified check-in yet</b></p><details><summary>Evidence history</summary><pre id="history">No evidence yet.</pre></details><details><summary>Laboratory boundaries</summary><p>The kit contains your signing key. Keep it private. This prototype sends it through the local adapter and is not suitable for production secrets. Witnesses run on one Docker host. Static custody shares can be misused by a malicious custody quorum.</p></details></aside></div><footer>No email, SMS, public destinations or real user data. The application displays protocol evidence; its database is disposable.</footer></main>
<script src="/solo.js"></script></html>
